.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "export_profiles" "export_profiles"
.SH NAME
export_profiles \- Write the mutant (and the control) expression profiles of a set of in silico perturbation
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIexport_profiles(\fBresults\fR as any, 
\fBfile\fR as string, 
\fBcontrolFile\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Write the mutant (and the control) expression profiles of a set of in silico perturbation
 results as csv matrix files.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBresults\fB \fR\- 
 a collection of the [InterventionResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.Intervention.InterventionResult) object, for example the value returned
 by the \fBknockouts\fR / \fBknockdown\fR / \fBoverexpress\fR api of the \fBbnlearn\fR package.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfile\fB \fR\- 
 the output file path of the mutant matrix (\fBmutant_means_matrix.csv\fR), rows are genes and
 columns are the intervention conditions.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBcontrolFile\fB \fR\- 
 the output file path of the control matrix; when it is nothing the file
 \fBwildtype_means_matrix.csv\fR is written next to **file**.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
TRUE when both matrix files have been written; an R# error message object is returned when
 the input can not be treated as a collection of [InterventionResult](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.BNLearn.Intervention.InterventionResult).
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The generated csv files use exactly the same layout as the ones produced by the
 \fBmake_exports\fR api (four comment lines followed by a \fBGene,<condition>...\fR header),
 but only the two matrices that are needed by the downstream submission builder are written;
 \fBmake_exports\fR writes about eight tables per run which is several gigabytes for a few
 hundred conditions.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GPS
